  "id": "DrugBank_DB09064 - MONDO_7759",
  "verbalization": "Ciprofibrate is implicated in the pathogenesis of Hyperlipidemia, Familial Combined, Lpl Related through a mechanism involving hypertriglyceridemia. The evidence suggests that Ciprofibrate, through its indication for Hypertriglyceridemia, activates downstream pathways that lead to hyperlipidemia. This is supported by the indication of Ciprofibrate for Hypertriglyceridemia, which in turn is linked to the use of Fenofibrate or Lovastatin or Pravastatin, all of which are known to influence lipid metabolism. These medications are commonly used to treat hyperlipidemia, and their association with the disease implies a shared mechanism of action. The integrated evidence highlights a potential link between Ciprofibrate and hyperlipidemia through its role in inducing hypertriglyceridemia, which is a key driver of the condition. The relationship is further supported by the overlapping pathways and the shared clinical outcomes, suggesting a plausible biological mechanism that connects Ciprofibrate to the development of familial combined hyperlipidemia.",
